\textcircled{2} \(\nu=4\) then \deleted{\(\unsure{K^g}=\operatorname{card}I^g=1\)} \inserted{\(K^g=\{P\}\)}, and \(I\setminus\{P\}\) is an orbit. We may suppose that it is \(\mu_4\), on which \(\mu_4\) acts, and \(P\) is a pole: \(\unsure{\infty}\). The full group of automorphisms is \(\mathbb Z/4\mathbb Z\simeq\mu_4(k)\).

The category of these configurations is equivalent to that of oriented squares.

\margin{``square pyramid''}
