\draw[->](-.55,.17)--(-.3,.17);
\end{tikzpicture}}

\textcircled{3} \(\nu=3\), Then \deleted{\(\unsure{K}\)} \(\operatorname{card}K^g=2\), \inserted{thus \(K^g=\Sigma^g\)}, and \(I\setminus K^g\) \inserted{\(=J\)} an orbit,
\deleted{The full group of}
which we may \unsure{suppose|take} to be \(\mu_3\). The category of these configurations is equivalent to that of combinatorial triangles, that is, the one \(\mathrm{Ens}(3)\) of sets \(J\) of cardinality \(3\).

To \(J\) we associate \(\Sigma_J\deleted{\unsure{\Sigma}}\) with \(J\cup P_J\) (\(P_J\subset\Sigma_J^{\unsure{g}}\) set of the two poles of \(\Sigma_J\) \unsure{for a|in} \(1\)-\(1\) correspondence with the set \(\omega(J)\) of orientations of \(J\), if \(\unsure{k|K}=\mathbb C\)). Group of automorphisms is \(\mathbb D_3\).

